<root class="tutorial" id="get-started">
  <h2>Get started in 60 seconds</h2>
  <ol class="tutorial-steps">
    <li class="tutorial-step">
      <span class="step-num">1</span>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Install the CLI</h3>
        <p>The <code>pocopine</code> CLI handles building, serving, and hot-reload — one install covers all three.</p>
<pre class="code-block"><code><span class="c-cmd">cargo</span> <span class="c-arg">install pocopine-cli</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="tutorial-step">
      <span class="step-num">2</span>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Scaffold an app</h3>
        <p>A pocopine app is a regular Rust library crate. Add <code>pocopine</code> (runtime) and <code>pine</code> (optional UI primitives).</p>
<pre class="code-block"><code><span class="c-cmd">cargo</span> <span class="c-arg">new --lib hello-pine</span>
<span class="c-cmd">cd</span> <span class="c-arg">hello-pine</span>
<span class="c-cmd">cargo</span> <span class="c-arg">add pocopine pine</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="tutorial-step">
      <span class="step-num">3</span>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Write your first component</h3>
        <p>A component is a Rust struct plus a sibling <code>.poco</code> template.</p>
<pre class="code-block"><code><span class="c-comment">// src/lib.rs</span>
<span class="c-cmd">use</span> pocopine::prelude::*;

<span class="c-cmd">#[derive(Default, Serialize, Deserialize)]</span>
<span class="c-cmd">#[component(template = </span><span class="c-str">"Counter.poco"</span><span class="c-cmd">)]</span>
<span class="c-cmd">pub struct</span> Counter { <span class="c-cmd">pub</span> n: u32 }

<span class="c-cmd">#[handlers]</span>
<span class="c-cmd">impl</span> Counter {
    <span class="c-cmd">pub fn</span> bump(&mut self) { self.n += 1; }
}

<span class="c-cmd">#[wasm_bindgen(start)]</span>
<span class="c-cmd">pub fn</span> main() {
    App::new().register::&lt;Counter&gt;().run();
}</code></pre>
<pre class="code-block"><code><span class="c-comment">&lt;!-- src/Counter.poco --&gt;</span>
&lt;button @click=<span class="c-str">"bump"</span>&gt;
  clicked &lt;strong pp-text=<span class="c-str">"n"</span>&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; times
&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="tutorial-step">
      <span class="step-num">4</span>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Run it</h3>
        <p><code>pocopine dev</code> builds the wasm bundle, serves it on a local port, and rebuilds on save. Ship with <code>pocopine build --release</code>.</p>
<pre class="code-block"><code><span class="c-cmd">pocopine</span> <span class="c-arg">dev</span>
<span class="c-comment"># → listening on http://127.0.0.1:5243</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</root>
